{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"MEASUREMENT CORRECTION AFFECTING EVERY REBAR NUMBER IN THE STUDY. Every rebar verdict reports a Sonnet model id at top level, which reads as rebar running on a weaker model than the CE and superpowers arms and would be a serious confound. The per-call usage log shows otherwise: the plan-reviewer calls, which are the review itself, run at the frontier model class on Opus, and Sonnet serves only the coach, prerequisite-verifier and agentic-verifier ops. The verdict field reports the LAST model used. No model handicap exists and every cross-arm number already reported stands. Do not cite the verdict model field as the review model; the authoritative source is the per-call usage log partitioned by op and model class. This had been sitting unexamined in all nine earlier verdicts."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789443044914136001,"uuid":"0d8f2a8e-fb67-4bef-8b8b-8b2ffed9b4cd"}